# Line-ending policy.
#
# Git decides per file whether it is text; every text file is stored with LF in the
# repository AND checked out with LF in the working tree, on every platform. This keeps
# the repo consistent with .editorconfig (end_of_line = lf) and prevents CRLF noise in
# diffs and in Prettier once the formatter lands in Milestone 1.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary: never normalized, never diffed as text.
# Corrupting a binary through line-ending translation is silent and unrecoverable.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.7z binary
*.xls binary
*.xlsx binary
*.mp3 binary
*.m4a binary
*.wav binary
*.webm binary
*.mp4 binary

# Generated lockfile: keep it in the repo, keep it out of review diffs.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true

# Security settings are committed byte-for-byte and are never rewritten by tooling,
# including by end-of-line normalization. Without this, the `* text=auto eol=lf` rule
# above marks the file as pending renormalization and invites a tool-driven rewrite of
# a file that only a human should change.
.claude/settings.json -text
